new file mode 100644
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/grouped-prefill.md
@@ -0,0 +1,50 @@
+# Grouped MLP prefill prototype
+
+`Model.prefill_chunked(input_ids, params, chunk_size)` shares MLP expert work across
+several supplied chunks. Each layer runs attention in causal chunk order, combines
+the normalized MLP inputs, computes the MLP once, then completes each chunk's
+residual update. Attention, normalization and residual mixing retain `chunk_size`.
+This gives streamed experts actual reuse within a layer and reduces weight transfers.
+
+The API accepts one local, rectangular, causal text prompt with a KV cache:
+
+```python
+model.prefill_chunked(input_ids, {
+    "attn_mode": "flash_attn",
+    "cache": cache,
+    "past_len": past_len,
+    "batch_shape": (1, cache_capacity),
+    "recurrent_states": recurrent_states,
+}, chunk_size=attention_chunk_size)
+```
+
+The caller must supply the future tokens being grouped. No predictions, stored
+expert profiles, model names, device names or pinned resident weight cache are used.
+Recurrent state types must explicitly support layer-major execution. Gated delta
+and short-convolution states do; states that depend on global position during
+individual layer execution are rejected. TP, paged batches, multimodal input,
+noncausal attention, recurrent history and state export are outside this prototype.
+The existing paged generator has not been migrated to this entrypoint.
+
+Group admission starts with a real physical chunk and records its workspace and
+activation geometry. Later calls use live free VRAM plus reusable allocator blocks,
+capped by physical device capacity. Additional group storage is estimated from the
+loaded MLP's tensor dimensions; attention/normalization workspace stays bounded.
+A prior allocator peak can make admission conservative. Estimates have been tested
+on the recorded workload, not exhaustively across every supported architecture.
+`auto_group=False` bypasses admission for explicit diagnostic groups.
+
+The performance CLI exposes `--grouped_prefill`. It preserves the ordinary workload's
+individual token slices, attention chunk limit, incremental length accounting and
+timing boundaries, including concatenation and admission overhead. Grouping increases
+the scheduler's prefill quantum and retains more activations; it does not increase
+the pinned expert weight budget.
+
+The accompanying piece-ring change sizes the pinned ring from detected per-domain
+L3 capacity and expert byte geometry. The bandwidth probe now completes its warmup
+window and retries until peak readings converge or its bounded retry budget ends.
+
+Validation and measurements are recorded in the enclosing investigation's
+`docs/analysis/2026-09-07-online-prefetch-worklog.md`. Numerical comparisons use repeated
+controls: greedy decoding can diverge at close token decisions even between controls,
+so fixed-continuation logits are also compared.
